Falsifies `designware_mobile_storage::proofs::an_extended_card_specific_data_sector_count_is_total`.

The defect: the sector count is read from bytes 211 to 214, one byte early, so it takes the top
byte of the reserved field before it and drops its own top byte. A short buffer of 215 bytes also
yields a count where the decoder owes zero.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that a buffer under 216 bytes gives 0, and its check that
216 bytes give the little-endian word at 212.

diff --git a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
--- a/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
+++ b/crates/designware_mobile_storage/src/card.rs
@@ -226,7 +226,7 @@
 #[doc(alias = "ext_csd")]
 #[must_use]
 pub(crate) fn extended_card_specific_data_sectors(extended_card_specific_data: &[u8]) -> u64 {
-    match extended_card_specific_data.get(212..216) {
+    match extended_card_specific_data.get(211..215) {
         Some(b) => u32::from_le_bytes([b[0], b[1], b[2], b[3]]) as u64,
         None => 0,
     }
